            "review_title": "Review at Nam Ranh Quan",
            "review_text": "WorldTravellerBC\nB.C.215 contributions\n0\nGood given the prices!\nNov 2023 • Family\nWe had asked where locals in Da Nang dine and this was one of the suggestions - we had no idea until our visit that all the dishes on the menu were fixed at 70000 Dong each; cash only. There was a wide range of dishes and truly some were hot and miss - but no complaints given the price of each dish. The highlight was ordering what we thought were scallops but the dish turned out to be stuffed clams - which were delicious! The experience was more enjoyable than the dishes we ordered - perhaps we might have chosen better if we had a local person with us?\n\nThe staff were friendly and tried to speak in English but it was a struggle - atmosphere was very \"local\" in our minds - open air indoor seating on shared tables. We had a late lunch/early dinner so missed what I suspect would be crowds. This restaurant is worth a visit if you are close by - not necessary to make a special trip.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 13, 2023",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
